WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:20.425
This motion picutre is an adaptation of the real life story of a historic figure.

2
00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:25.425
Although artistic license has been taken, the essence of the story remains true...

3
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:29.047
...to the events that continue to inspire generations.

4
00:00:29.091 --> 00:00:31.010
It remains one of the oldest accounts of humanity's struggle equality & freedom.

5
00:00:34.945 --> 00:00:38.356
<b><font color="#FF8080>  Bilal </font></b>

6
00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:48.356
Inspired by a true story

7
00:00:51.886 --> 00:00:53.234
A film by : Ayman Jamal

8
00:01:02.117 --> 00:01:19.842
Enjoy!

9
00:01:30.117 --> 00:01:37.842
Translation and synchronizing
<font color="#F76541">  Ikraam </font>

10
00:03:20.028 --> 00:03:21.873
BILAL: Ghufaira!

11
00:03:32.459 --> 00:03:33.276
MOTHER: Ah, ah, ah...

12
00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:19.727
Oh!

13
00:04:23.606 --> 00:04:25.297
Mother, who are they?

14
00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:35.057
Mother!

15
00:04:35.763 --> 00:04:37.215
Keep your sister safe, Bilal.

16
00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:47.893
No!

17
00:05:35.502 --> 00:05:36.864
GHUFAIRA: Bilal.

18
00:05:36.994 --> 00:05:38.346
Are you alright?

19
00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:40.112
- I am fine.

20
00:05:40.295 --> 00:05:42.563
- Was it... that dream again ?

21
00:05:44.511 --> 00:05:45.816
Here.

22
00:05:46.353 --> 00:05:47.613
I was saving this for you.

23
00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:51.204
- There's a piece of it missing.

24
00:05:51.212 --> 00:05:53.946
- Well, I'm waiting.

25
00:05:57.326 --> 00:06:00.845
- Oh, (chuckles) why thank you my wonderful 
amazing, sister.

26
00:06:01.215 --> 00:06:03.477
- You are very welcome my loving brother.

27
00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:04.504
That is more like it.

28
00:06:05.249 --> 00:06:06.342
- What can one Dirham (sliver piece) buy?

29
00:06:06.671 --> 00:06:07.265
- Well, to start...

30
00:06:07.271 --> 00:06:10.365
...a blessing! From one of the Gods!

31
00:06:10.369 --> 00:06:13.917
Maybe one of them will bring you 
something to stop your nightmares.

32
00:06:14.024 --> 00:06:16.699
- Where were these Gods when Mother
needed them?

33
00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:20.291
I will buy you something sweet to eat instead. <i>(BANG)</i>

34
00:06:20.489 --> 00:06:22.869
GUARD: Ghufaira, fetch water for the master!

35
00:06:22.901 --> 00:06:24.159
Move it!

36
00:06:27.093 --> 00:06:28.251
I'll get it.

37
00:06:50.265 --> 00:06:52.815
<i>(shouts in the markets) </i>

38
00:07:00.417 --> 00:07:03.703
<i>(yells) Spices, spices!</i>

39
00:07:04.524 --> 00:07:09.011
<i>(more shouts)</i>

40
00:07:22.982 --> 00:07:25.874
Different colours, different prices.
How much it has been?

41
00:07:25.982 --> 00:07:27.874
<i>(metals clanging) </i>

42
00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:31.880
<i>(offers) Would you like to taste one? </i>

43
00:07:32.364 --> 00:07:33.566
OKBA: Idols for sale!

44
00:07:33.596 --> 00:07:35.048
Idols for sale!

45
00:07:35.868 --> 00:07:37.917
They come in all colors and shapes!

46
00:07:38.421 --> 00:07:40.218
And make your wishes comes true!

47
00:07:40.343 --> 00:07:41.829
Idols for fame!

48
00:07:42.584 --> 00:07:43.625
Idols for strength!

49
00:07:44.382 --> 00:07:45.863
Idols for fertility!

50
00:07:46.257 --> 00:07:47.787
Idols for beauty!

51
00:07:49.303 --> 00:07:53.115
I can see that you definitely don't 
need an idol for beauty.

52
00:07:53.725 --> 00:07:56.112
The idol needs you. <i>(laughs)</i>

53
00:07:59.725 --> 00:08:00.712
- Thank you.

54
00:08:00.953 --> 00:08:01.840
- But, for fertility!

55
00:08:02.572 --> 00:08:04.117
You want to bear a son, don't you?

56
00:08:05.247 --> 00:08:07.575
With this, you can bear triplets! <i>(laughs)</i>

57
00:08:11.489 --> 00:08:12.813
<i>(camels grunt)</i>

58
00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:14.232
<i>(shouts in the markets) Sweets!</i>

59
00:08:19.172 --> 00:08:20.503
<i>(people greeting) Good morning, my brother!</i>

60
00:08:26.113 --> 00:08:27.756
<i>(warns) Watch where you going boy!</i>

61
00:08:50.554 --> 00:08:51.531
<i>(shouts from afar)</i>

62
00:09:02.528 --> 00:09:06.183
CHARLATAN PRIEST: The idols see all!

63
00:09:08.986 --> 00:09:12.516
The idols know all!

64
00:09:16.643 --> 00:09:18.660
Stray not into the desert sands!

65
00:09:19.796 --> 00:09:22.317
Lest the harsh flames of wrath consume you!

66
00:09:23.514 --> 00:09:25.027
Come, enter!

67
00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:28.337
Prove your faith with wealth and gifts!

68
00:09:29.723 --> 00:09:32.054
Appease the idols and Gods...

69
00:09:32.741 --> 00:09:35.710
Or else...

70
00:09:36.253 --> 00:09:38.073
<i>(deep whispers) </i>

71
00:09:40.656 --> 00:09:41.760
Come, boy!

72
00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:43.431
Come!

73
00:09:44.017 --> 00:09:45.574
You wish to be free of nightmares...

74
00:09:46.646 --> 00:09:47.843
Don't you?

75
00:09:50.175 --> 00:09:52.003
Take that coin from your pocket...

76
00:09:54.215 --> 00:09:55.815
<i>(deep whispers) </i>

77
00:09:59.028 --> 00:10:00.069
No offering too small...

78
00:10:01.486 --> 00:10:02.999
No wish too big...

79
00:10:04.763 --> 00:10:07.064
You can have...

80
00:10:07.475 --> 00:10:09.870
...whatever you desire!

81
00:10:22.343 --> 00:10:24.519
The idols see all...

82
00:10:31.548 --> 00:10:31.738
<i> (panting & mumbling) </i>

83
00:10:55.164 --> 00:10:56.354
SIDEKICK: You missed!

84
00:10:57.437 --> 00:10:58.595
SAFWAN: On purpose.

85
00:11:00.117 --> 00:11:02.940
My arrows need worthy target.

86
00:11:03.398 --> 00:11:05.540
I wouldn't waste them on a chicken.

87
00:11:07.557 --> 00:11:09.314
But a deer...

88
00:11:10.273 --> 00:11:12.892
Where would we find a deer?

89
00:11:23.974 --> 00:11:24.167
What?

90
00:11:24.558 --> 00:11:26.844
S-safwan, what are you doing?

91
00:11:29.202 --> 00:11:29.951
Safwan!

92
00:11:33.897 --> 00:11:34.843
There's a deer...

93
00:11:36.198 --> 00:11:37.325
...a black one.

94
00:11:41.416 --> 00:11:42.803
Over here, slave!

95
00:11:45.092 --> 00:11:47.364
I said, come here!

96
00:11:48.066 --> 00:11:49.284
Stop, slave!

97
00:11:50.039 --> 00:11:51.300
I command you!

98
00:12:00.492 --> 00:12:02.099
<i>(chuckles)</i> The deer thinks it's a lion.

99
00:12:02.974 --> 00:12:04.172
- Yeah, you better watch out! <i>(growls)</i>

100
00:12:05.056 --> 00:12:06.411
- You, better watch out!

101
00:12:06.966 --> 00:12:07.792
- Aa-I was kidding.

102
00:12:07.793 --> 00:12:08.793
- Shut up!

103
00:12:09.393 --> 00:12:10.844
Now, get her.

104
00:12:16.903 --> 00:12:19.534
GHUFAIRA: Let go!

105
00:12:23.801 --> 00:12:24.841
- Don't move.

106
00:12:26.015 --> 00:12:26.772
- Don't, please don't!

107
00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:31.775
BILAL: No!

108
00:12:42.447 --> 00:12:44.684
<i>(laughs)</i> Safwan, looks like 
you got your deer...

109
00:12:45.607 --> 00:12:46.897
...in his tail!

110
00:12:51.898 --> 00:12:53.008
- You will not harm her !

111
00:12:53.077 --> 00:12:53.795
- How dare you give me an order?

112
00:12:55.434 --> 00:12:57.072
Teach this rat a lesson!

113
00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:48.477
GHUFAIRA: Please forgive him
master Safwan!

114
00:13:55.070 --> 00:13:57.428
IDOL MAKER: Hey, what are you 
boys doing?

115
00:14:00.073 --> 00:14:03.187
Oh, I-I didn't know it was you,
young master Safwan.

116
00:14:03.803 --> 00:14:05.089
Apologies.

117
00:14:05.216 --> 00:14:07.049
Are these slaves bothering you?

118
00:14:07.472 --> 00:14:09.823
I'll thrash them, if they are!

119
00:14:14.578 --> 00:14:14.895
Come on, let's go.

120
00:14:14.878 --> 00:14:17.806
- Tell your father, I'll deliver his 
order today!

121
00:14:21.048 --> 00:14:21.703
BILAL: Ghufaira!

122
00:14:22.587 --> 00:14:23.533
Did they hurt you? Oh...

123
00:14:24.796 --> 00:14:27.022
I should have been here to protect you.

124
00:14:28.064 --> 00:14:30.453
I will never let anyone hurt you 
ever again.

125
00:14:40.001 --> 00:14:40.975
<i>BLACK MARKET MERCHANT: 
Step forward! Patience!</i>

126
00:14:40.996 --> 00:14:42.376
<i>(competing shouts)</i>
<i>Make your offer.</i>

127
00:14:42.377 --> 00:14:43.977
<i>And this prized specimen shall 
be yours!</i>

128
00:14:45.221 --> 00:14:45.978
<i>Do i hear 2nd on that?<i/>

129
00:14:47.221 --> 00:14:48.978
<i>3rd? Sold, sold!</i>

130
00:14:50.457 --> 00:14:52.873
<i>Get this wretch out of here!</i>

131
00:15:01.357 --> 00:15:03.209
OKBA: This is the finest slave in 
my possession

132
00:15:04.038 --> 00:15:06.549
He's clever, he reads and writes!

133
00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:09.637
He speaks twenty languages.

134
00:15:10.333 --> 00:15:11.468
Twenty i say! <i>(laughs)</i>

135
00:15:14.401 --> 00:15:16.606
<i>(snake hissing)</i>
He even speaks to animals!

136
00:15:18.401 --> 00:15:20.229
Oh, great Umayya!

137
00:15:21.018 --> 00:15:24.483
You can't ask for a better servant
on your trading missions, oh no...

138
00:15:28.014 --> 00:15:29.649
Ah! That one is not quite as clever...

139
00:15:30.878 --> 00:15:32.171
...but he is as strong as rocks!

140
00:15:37.649 --> 00:15:38.313
UMAYYA: I'll take him.

141
00:15:38.314 --> 00:15:39.314
- You will?

142
00:15:41.054 --> 00:15:43.355
I-I-I mean, e-excellent choice!

143
00:15:44.688 --> 00:15:48.962
He's a bit expensive, but I know
the gods has been generous to you...

144
00:15:50.057 --> 00:15:51.381
...my dearest Umayya!

145
00:15:55.388 --> 00:15:56.863
- Okba...

146
00:15:56.838 --> 00:15:59.730
...one of these days, I'm gonna dip 
your tongue in a bowl of dry sand.

147
00:16:01.415 --> 00:16:02.329
Have him delivered.

148
00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:09.134
- Oh, thank you, thank you, thank you!

149
00:16:10.017 --> 00:16:10.648
Thank you! <i>(laughs)</i>

150
00:16:11.759 --> 00:16:13.642
Ah! Blessed Umayya! <i>(laughs)</i>

151
00:16:14.968 --> 00:16:16.388
Gracious! Magnificent! <i>(laughs)</i>

152
00:16:23.175 --> 00:16:23.900
IDOL MAKER: Your honor!

153
00:16:24.627 --> 00:16:26.139
I have the Idols you ordered.

154
00:16:26.613 --> 00:16:28.757
Should I bring them to your home
or the shop at the market ?

155
00:16:29.641 --> 00:16:30.241
-What do you think ?

156
00:16:34.336 --> 00:16:36.010
The market you idiot!

157
00:16:36.369 --> 00:16:37.961
And the next time you are late...

158
00:16:38.079 --> 00:16:40.353
...I won't pay.

159
00:16:40.929 --> 00:16:41.970
- A thousand pardons.

160
00:16:42.295 --> 00:16:43.738
It won't happen again!

161
00:16:44.652 --> 00:16:47.645
I-I was delayed. I-I had to come to
the aid of your son...

162
00:16:48.002 --> 00:16:48.995
...Safwan!

163
00:16:50.443 --> 00:16:51.792
- Hmm? What about Safwan?

164
00:16:51.801 --> 00:16:53.817
- He was being assaulted, by 
a slave boy!

165
00:16:54.021 --> 00:16:55.177
- Which slave ?

166
00:16:55.680 --> 00:16:56.998
- They called him Bilal.

167
00:16:57.639 --> 00:16:58.994
He-he had your son on the ground!

168
00:16:58.999 --> 00:17:00.007 
But I, I pull him up.

169
00:17:00.495 --> 00:17:01.907
Saved him from a thrashing!

170
00:17:02.086 --> 00:17:03.111
- Enough!

171
00:17:04.173 --> 00:17:05.514
Take these idols to my store at once...

172
00:17:05.715 --> 00:17:07.139
...or forget the deal.

173
00:17:07.585 --> 00:17:09.096
- Yes sir, of course!

174
00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:10.078
Right away.

175
00:17:14.770 --> 00:17:15.307
UMAYYA: Bilal!

176
00:17:28.007 --> 00:17:29.693
Pick it up.

177
00:17:31.269 --> 00:17:34.224
I said, pick it up.

178
00:17:54.054 --> 00:17:55.504
Whose apple is this?

179
00:17:55.714 --> 00:17:56.737
Whose is it?

180
00:17:57.393 --> 00:17:58.759
BILAL: Yours sir, yours.

181
00:17:58.898 --> 00:18:02.895
- And what is the difference
between you and this apple?

182
00:18:02.973 --> 00:18:03.953
- No difference, sir.
<i>(grunts)</i>

183
00:18:10.865 --> 00:18:12.000
- Don't you forget it again.

184
00:18:13.710 --> 00:18:15.593
Take him out to the courtyard...

185
00:18:16.381 --> 00:18:17.481
...and whip him.

186
00:18:21.982 --> 00:18:22.982
GUARD: Move!

187
00:18:25.994 --> 00:18:29.008
SAFWAN: No matter what you do...

188
00:18:30.492 --> 00:18:33.423
...a master breeds a master...

189
00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:36.690
...and a slave breeds a slave.

190
00:18:44.555 --> 00:18:48.862
Father, I hope you're going to teach him
a lesson he'll never...

191
00:18:48.971 --> 00:18:50.721
- How could you let a slave beat you?

192
00:18:53.172 --> 00:18:54.214
- Bilal's lying, father!

193
00:18:54.815 --> 00:18:55.887
The slave is lying.

194
00:18:56.550 --> 00:18:57.591
He did not beat... (smacks)

195
00:18:58.075 --> 00:18:59.799
- You make me look like a fool.

196
00:19:02.259 --> 00:19:03.426
Stop it!

197
00:19:04.027 --> 00:19:05.036
Stop it I say!

198
00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:07.653
Listen.

199
00:19:11.645 --> 00:19:13.213
He's isn't crying...

200
00:19:14.034 --> 00:19:15.452
...and you shouldn't be crying either.

201
00:19:17.745 --> 00:19:18.596
I dont care what happened...

202
00:19:19.292 --> 00:19:23.197
...don't ever let a slave embarrass
me in public, again.

203
00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:26.726
<i>(whips)</i>

204
00:20:40.798 --> 00:20:48.469
BILAL: Mother, what kind of man
was my father?

205
00:20:49.014 --> 00:20:50.244
MOTHER: Your father was a great man.

206
00:20:51.379 --> 00:20:54.144
What do you want to be when
you grow up Bilal?

207
00:20:55.568 --> 00:20:56.074
A farmer?

208
00:20:56.987 --> 00:20:59.603
Or may be a merchant that makes
a lot of money?

209
00:21:00.446 --> 00:21:03.368
- Ha! I want to be a great warrior!

210
00:21:05.424 --> 00:21:09.126
<i>(laughs)</i> - And that's what you will be,
a great warrior.

211
00:21:11.089 --> 00:21:12.480
With a beautiful voice.

212
00:21:12.582 --> 00:21:14.626
- And I want to ride a big horse.

213
00:21:15.481 --> 00:21:16.899
And I will fight enemies...

214
00:21:17.027 --> 00:21:19.232
...and protect you, and Ghufaira.

215
00:21:19.233 --> 00:21:21.433
- That's very honourable, Bilal.

216
00:21:22.414 --> 00:21:23.763
But, remember...

217
00:21:24.027 --> 00:21:26.032
...a sword and a horse...

218
00:21:26.067 --> 00:21:27.748
...cannot make you a great man.

219
00:21:28.507 --> 00:21:28.825
- They can't?

220
00:21:28.990 --> 00:21:29.776
- No.

221
00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:31.448
Being a great man,

222
00:21:32.395 --> 00:21:34.317
...means living without chains

223
00:21:36.712 --> 00:21:37.187
- Huh, chains?

224
00:21:37.379 --> 00:21:40.608
- No, (chuckles) the ones you can't see...

225
00:21:41.766 --> 00:21:43.405
...the ones in here.

226
00:21:44.023 --> 00:21:45.301
- Inside me?

227
00:21:48.513 --> 00:21:49.774
- Being a warrior,

228
00:21:50.408 --> 00:21:52.330
...wont make you a great man,

229
00:21:53.150 --> 00:21:56.174
...if you are chained to anger
and vengeance.

230
00:21:57.489 --> 00:21:59.852
Superstition and fear are chains too,

231
00:22:00.579 --> 00:22:02.091
...and there are others.

232
00:22:03.803 --> 00:22:06.008
To be a great man,

233
00:22:06.989 --> 00:22:09.322
...you have to break free of them all.

234
00:22:09.923 --> 00:22:11.027
- But how I do I do that?

235
00:22:11.597 --> 00:22:13.067
I can't see inside me.

236
00:22:13.840 --> 00:22:14.251
- I can...

237
00:22:15.716 --> 00:22:18.047
...and I see the heart of a great man, Bilal.

238
00:22:20.034 --> 00:22:23.151
You'll find the way. Guidance will come.

239
00:22:24.163 --> 00:22:24.609
You'll see.

240
00:22:25.586 --> 00:22:28.754
No chains will hold to you.

241
00:22:29.355 --> 00:22:31.595
No chains...

242
00:22:36.816 --> 00:22:38.138
BILAL: You were wrong, mother.

243
00:22:38.809 --> 00:22:40.735
I am a slave.

244
00:22:40.736 --> 00:22:44.736
And I will always be in chain.

245
00:22:54.541 --> 00:22:58.041 
GHUFAIRA: (gasps) Why did they have
to whip you?

246
00:22:58.308 --> 00:23:00.039
You didn't do anything!

247
00:23:00.171 --> 00:23:01.996
- It does not matter.

248
00:23:02.078 --> 00:23:04.089
Master Umayya can do whatever he
wants with us.

249
00:23:04.531 --> 00:23:05.037
- Bilal!

250
00:23:19.027 --> 00:23:20.480
Look at what I found.

251
00:23:20.711 --> 00:23:23.078
I know you didn't mean to lose this!

252
00:23:23.161 --> 00:23:26.086
You can still use it to make an offering.

253
00:23:26.142 --> 00:23:27.542
I heard the Priest said;

254
00:23:28.056 --> 00:23:29.549
"Big blessing can come from small gifts."

255
00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:31.086
- I don't need it.

256
00:23:31.516 --> 00:23:34.404
I am never gonna hope for anything again.

257
00:23:35.081 --> 00:23:36.386
I am a Slave!

258
00:23:36.467 --> 00:23:39.081
And no God in the market has the power
to change that!

259
00:23:40.987 --> 00:23:43.461
- Alright. I'll keep it.

260
00:23:43.533 --> 00:23:45.922
And i won't spend it either.

261
00:23:45.980 --> 00:23:47.021
It's yours.

262
00:23:47.194 --> 00:23:50.686
I'll keep it safe for you until 
you ask for it back.

263
00:25:27.060 --> 00:25:28.376
BILAL: Very funny!

264
00:27:43.248 --> 00:27:46.917
BILAL: <i>No, no, no!</i>

265
00:27:56.046 --> 00:27:57.026
SAAD: (laughs) <i>The way you fly off
that horse...</i>

266
00:27:57.153 --> 00:28:00.231
...amazes me every single time.

267
00:28:00.256 --> 00:28:01.222
It never gets old!

268
00:28:03.578 --> 00:28:05.881
- (laughs) It's only been twice...

269
00:28:06.056 --> 00:28:07.469
...today!

270
00:28:15.920 --> 00:28:18.276
- I, on the other hand...

271
00:28:18.277 --> 00:28:19.777
...never miss.

272
00:28:20.173 --> 00:28:23.187
- You just love to show off,
don't you Saad?

273
00:28:23.337 --> 00:28:26.003
Besides, you have all the time and 
money to practice.

274
00:28:27.562 --> 00:28:31.466
- You need more than money to
be the best of what you do.

275
00:28:31.570 --> 00:28:34.024
You need a great deal of determination.

276
00:28:34.570 --> 00:28:35.324
- Ha, right !

277
00:28:35.479 --> 00:28:38.535
So your determination is to hunt fruit?

278
00:28:38.835 --> 00:28:40.035
I have to get back.

279
00:28:40.174 --> 00:28:41.090
Believe me,

280
00:28:41.305 --> 00:28:44.087
...you do not want to upset
master Umayya.

281
00:28:46.501 --> 00:28:49.064
- Tell me something, Bilal.

282
00:28:49.143 --> 00:28:52.067
Why don't you just start riding
and keep on going?

283
00:28:52.345 --> 00:28:55.038
Cross those dunes to whatever
they may lead?

284
00:28:55.568 --> 00:28:57.683
- And find my palace?

285
00:28:57.818 --> 00:29:00.075
More likely I'd find it...

286
00:29:00.112 --> 00:29:02.094
...only to end up working in it.

287
00:29:02.330 --> 00:29:05.002
See you later, 'Apple hunter'.

288
00:29:17.056 --> 00:29:18.782
SAAD: <i>Here, for your troubles.</i>

289
00:29:18.798 --> 00:29:19.802
Till next time, my friend.

290
00:29:42.820 --> 00:29:45.776
CHILD: Please, get a little bit of coin ?

291
00:29:46.128 --> 00:29:48.742
Please, I want some food, some coins.

292
00:29:49.142 --> 00:29:50.897
Please? (sighs)

293
00:29:52.064 --> 00:29:54.199
Please, some coins?
- MAN: Out of the way child!

294
00:29:55.154 --> 00:29:58.237
- Please, I have no food.

295
00:29:59.237 --> 00:30:01.005
(sighs)

295.1
00:30:36.237 --> 00:30:40.005
BILAL: No...

296
00:30:42.108 --> 00:30:44.467
...you do not want to do that.

297
00:30:52.095 --> 00:30:54.400
- But I'm so hungry.

298
00:30:55.040 --> 00:30:56.508
- Here,

299
00:30:56.995 --> 00:30:58.945
...take this.

300
00:31:03.965 --> 00:31:06.764
- You're so kind.

301
00:31:20.490 --> 00:31:25.043
AL-SIDDIQ: <i>You would rather pay for your 
own pocket than to see this god losing wealth?</i>

302
00:31:25.143 --> 00:31:27.294
- I wanted to spare the boy a beating.

303
00:31:28.549 --> 00:31:31.386
- Ah, then you care more for a beggar boy...

304
00:31:31.454 --> 00:31:33.509
...than an idol?

305
00:31:33.681 --> 00:31:36.824
Don't you believe 
the promises of the priest?

306
00:31:37.999 --> 00:31:39.467
- My apologies, sir.

307
00:31:39.567 --> 00:31:40.768
I am just a slave.

308
00:31:40.795 --> 00:31:41.941
I know no better.

309
00:31:42.314 --> 00:31:43.914
- Don't you?

310
00:31:47.245 --> 00:31:49.233
Or do you?

311
00:31:49.333 --> 00:31:51.051
- You're no priest.

312
00:31:51.625 --> 00:31:54.622
You're... the lord of merchants.

313
00:31:55.230 --> 00:31:56.509
Al-Sadiq! (Abu Bakr) 

314
00:31:56.845 --> 00:31:58.818
- Indeed.

315
00:31:58.975 --> 00:32:02.004
Are you kneeling because you thought
I was a priest?

316
00:32:02.104 --> 00:32:05.915
Or was it my question that
frightened you ?

317
00:32:05.949 --> 00:32:09.006
Get up son, do not be afraid.

318
00:32:10.686 --> 00:32:13.989
- (chuckles) No, sir I'm not frightened.

319
00:32:14.755 --> 00:32:15.868
- You seem amused?

320
00:32:16.279 --> 00:32:20.098
- Your honor, what do you know about fear?

321
00:32:20.207 --> 00:32:23.038
- I have seen enough of it in the eyes of the
people.

322
00:32:23.348 --> 00:32:28.786
Enough to understand what make slaves of 
the many.

323
00:32:30.056 --> 00:32:32.106
<i>A woman is afraid she will bear a girl...</i>

324
00:32:32.242 --> 00:32:36.051
<i>...she pays an offering and begs...</i>

325
00:32:36.151 --> 00:32:37.060
<i>...to idols to fix it.</i>

326
00:32:37.565 --> 00:32:40.095
<i>A rich man fears poverty...</i>

327
00:32:40.106 --> 00:32:44.150
<i>...he shares a little
of his money with the Gods...</i>

328
00:32:44.293 --> 00:32:47.621
<i>...and promises more if they
help him to stay wealthy.</i>

329
00:32:47.721 --> 00:32:50.260
<i>An old man fears death...</i>

330
00:32:50.308 --> 00:32:53.300
<i>...so he pays a priest for deliverance.</i>

331
00:32:54.044 --> 00:33:00.017
<i>This fear compells them to seek
refuge in these Gods.</i>

332
00:33:01.004 --> 00:33:03.287
<i>Gods of greed, of injustice...</i>

333
00:33:04.788 --> 00:33:08.660
<i>...with hope that all their problems will go away.</i>

334
00:33:09.017 --> 00:33:12.099
Surely the sacred structure was not built 
to house for all of this corruption.

335
00:33:12.384 --> 00:33:13.488
It was built...

336
00:33:13.837 --> 00:33:16.443
...so that all mankind could stand together...

337
00:33:17.011 --> 00:33:18.731
...as equals...

338
00:33:19.073 --> 00:33:21.002
...and follow the One Creator.

339
00:33:21.202 --> 00:33:22.503
- Except for slaves.

340
00:33:22.703 --> 00:33:23.458
- Son...

341
00:33:23.658 --> 00:33:26.234
...no one is born a slave.

342
00:33:26.434 --> 00:33:27.411
You were free once...

343
00:33:27.553 --> 00:33:29.040
...were you not?

344
00:33:29.740 --> 00:33:33.053
- I was, once...

345
00:33:33.498 --> 00:33:36.621
...a long time ago.

346
00:33:37.283 --> 00:33:39.460
Devils raided my village...

347
00:33:39.660 --> 00:33:41.983
...destroyed my home.

348
00:33:42.183 --> 00:33:45.015
They took me, and Ghufaira...

349
00:33:45.115 --> 00:33:46.971
...my sister.

350
00:33:47.071 --> 00:33:48.621
- What about your...

351
00:33:48.721 --> 00:33:51.766
- She still talks to me.

352
00:33:51.966 --> 00:33:54.099
Sir...

353
00:33:54.099 --> 00:33:56.971
...all this talk of equality...

354
00:33:57.471 --> 00:33:58.401
...is wishful thinking.

355
00:33:58.501 --> 00:34:01.037
It holds no meaning to me.

356
00:34:01.137 --> 00:34:04.953
So save your speech for a man
who can afford this...

357
00:34:05.302 --> 00:34:06.438
...thing you are selling.

358
00:34:06.692 --> 00:34:07.607
- Young man!

359
00:34:08.112 --> 00:34:09.665
Life is more generous than you may think.

360
00:34:09.776 --> 00:34:12.238
I am not here to sell you anything.

361
00:34:12.386 --> 00:34:13.432
- It maybe sir...

362
00:34:13.574 --> 00:34:15.395
...but not for slaves.

363
00:34:17.622 --> 00:34:19.947
My master is expecting this.

364
00:34:20.533 --> 00:34:21.333
I must return.

365
00:34:21.933 --> 00:34:23.166
-Whom do you serve?

366
00:34:23.548 --> 00:34:24.717
- Master Umayya.

367
00:34:25.033 --> 00:34:27.015
The greatest man in the city.

368
00:34:27.115 --> 00:34:28.760
- And what is your name, son?

369
00:34:28.778 --> 00:34:29.960
- Bilal.

370
00:34:30.370 --> 00:34:31.002
- Bilal!

371
00:34:31.202 --> 00:34:35.354
I saw greatness in the hand
that saved that boy today.

372
00:34:35.554 --> 00:34:37.327
And remember...

373
00:34:37.427 --> 00:34:38.909
...great men are those who have...

374
00:34:38.919 --> 00:34:41.309
...the will to choose their own destiny.

375
00:34:52.457 --> 00:34:53.678
<i>GUARD: Yalla (let's go), hurry up!</i>

376
00:34:55.004 --> 00:34:56.108
<i> Hurry up, move it!</i>

377
00:34:56.738 --> 00:34:57.750
<i> Right now, faster! </i>

378
00:34:58.506 --> 00:34:59.484
<i> (whips) </i>

379
00:35:02.289 --> 00:35:03.363
<i> (screams) </i>

380
00:35:39.285 --> 00:35:41.168
SOLDIER: Good job, sir.

381
00:35:44.611 --> 00:35:45.898
Sir?

382
00:35:46.851 --> 00:35:48.830
BILAL: Master Safwan!

383
00:35:51.336 --> 00:35:52.866
Master Safwan...

384
00:35:52.948 --> 00:35:54.153
...your father summons you.

385
00:36:02.677 --> 00:36:05.600
SAFWAN: How many times do I have to remind you?

386
00:36:05.690 --> 00:36:08.155
Kneel when you come before me, slave.

387
00:36:09.267 --> 00:36:10.774
Kneel!

388
00:36:16.360 --> 00:36:18.937
Few were born to rule...

389
00:36:19.237 --> 00:36:21.144
...others, to serve.

390
00:36:30.638 --> 00:36:33.250
SOHEIB: You do not look good on your knees, brother.

391
00:36:33.950 --> 00:36:34.890
Get up my friend!

392
00:36:35.090 --> 00:36:37.043
You need to see what I got
for the feast tonight...

393
00:36:37.443 --> 00:36:38.737
...you will love it!

394
00:36:50.011 --> 00:36:51.310
GHUFAIRA: Where is he?

395
00:36:55.756 --> 00:36:57.391
You are late!

396
00:36:58.564 --> 00:36:59.964
- (chuckles) You remember my sister...

397
00:37:00.080 --> 00:37:01.091
...Ghufaira?

398
00:37:01.152 --> 00:37:02.273
- My lady...

399
00:37:02.416 --> 00:37:04.678
I am Soheib.

400
00:37:05.086 --> 00:37:07.105
A first grade Slave...

401
00:37:07.422 --> 00:37:09.030
...and blacksmith extraordinare.

402
00:37:09.179 --> 00:37:11.178
- (chuckles) Yes, a funny man.

403
00:37:11.312 --> 00:37:13.070
- Where were you?

404
00:37:13.152 --> 00:37:14.623
It almost time for the feast.

405
00:37:14.780 --> 00:37:16.673
They will whip you if you are late.

406
00:37:16.723 --> 00:37:18.345
No way.

407
00:37:18.437 --> 00:37:21.056
The master told me to fetch Safwan.

408
00:37:22.829 --> 00:37:24.650
- Did he harm you?

409
00:37:27.652 --> 00:37:31.037
- I would've turned this Safwan into 
a sac of potatoes...

410
00:37:31.050 --> 00:37:33.381
...if I'd only got there sooner.

411
00:37:33.474 --> 00:37:35.273
That princess!

412
00:37:35.719 --> 00:37:37.421
He and that little goon who follows 
him.

413
00:37:37.776 --> 00:37:40.452
You must remain strong, Bilal.

414
00:37:40.597 --> 00:37:43.856
They are only as strong as
the fear they put inside us.

415
00:37:45.016 --> 00:37:47.294
We must never give in.

416
00:37:47.397 --> 00:37:49.092
- (chuckles) Alright, back to work.

417
00:37:49.502 --> 00:37:50.545
- Behold...

418
00:37:50.645 --> 00:37:52.061
...special delivery...

419
00:37:52.129 --> 00:37:54.425
...to your master from my master.

420
00:37:56.357 --> 00:37:58.619
- (gasps) That's very shiny!

421
00:37:58.932 --> 00:38:00.479
- Hmm, nice work Soheib.

422
00:38:01.029 --> 00:38:03.884
- (chuckles) Yes, it's my finest one yet.

423
00:38:10.572 --> 00:38:12.834
MAN: <i>That's right, it's 
out sadiq (friend).</i>

424
00:38:12.934 --> 00:38:14.822
<i>I cannot believe!</i>

425
00:38:15.232 --> 00:38:17.975
This man goes about us, speaking
against the Gods.

426
00:38:18.275 --> 00:38:19.804
Every day!

427
00:38:19.904 --> 00:38:20.626
<i>Every day!</i>

428
00:38:21.130 --> 00:38:22.675
<i>How many followed him, 
I do not know.</i>

429
00:38:25.929 --> 00:38:28.539
ABU AL-HAKAM: You leave too 
much exposed.

430
00:38:28.754 --> 00:38:31.315
You relied too much on luck.

431
00:38:33.974 --> 00:38:36.160
UMAYYA: Luck favors the bold.

432
00:38:36.996 --> 00:38:38.348
- Perhaps.

433
00:38:38.793 --> 00:38:40.811
But are you willing to risk it at
the real world?

434
00:38:41.347 --> 00:38:43.744
- You ask as if you dont know me.

435
00:38:43.853 --> 00:38:44.785
- I ask...

436
00:38:44.889 --> 00:38:47.685
...because I see a threat looming.

437
00:38:47.859 --> 00:38:50.366
- You are truly obsessed with this nonsense.

438
00:38:50.465 --> 00:38:54.310
- This nonsense can strike you
where you stand, Umayya!

439
00:38:54.446 --> 00:38:55.970
Let's makes an example out of them...

440
00:38:56.018 --> 00:38:58.400
...a reminder to those who 
dare stand against us!

441
00:39:00.074 --> 00:39:03.804
After all,
we have a business to take care of.

442
00:39:05.509 --> 00:39:07.966
- Abu Al-Hakam! As always, you've managed...

443
00:39:08.040 --> 00:39:10.016
...to ruin my evening with your concerns.

444
00:39:11.529 --> 00:39:12.602
Bilal!

445
00:39:13.090 --> 00:39:14.434
Come, sing for us!

446
00:39:15.025 --> 00:39:16.897
Let's lighten the mood.

447
00:39:16.905 --> 00:39:20.301
OKBA: Ah, yes! I-I have heard my slaves speaking
of the...

448
00:39:20.405 --> 00:39:22.114
...swirlest voice.

449
00:39:22.256 --> 00:39:24.182
Lets hear it!

450
00:39:29.074 --> 00:39:33.479
<i># Distant shadows, #</i>

451
00:39:34.016 --> 00:39:37.864
<i># Mountains and trees. #</i>

452
00:39:38.077 --> 00:39:41.489
<i># Here I stand, #</i>

453
00:39:42.214 --> 00:39:45.304
<i># As she shelters me. #</i>

454
00:39:46.011 --> 00:39:50.063
<i># Distant shadows, #</i>

455
00:39:51.324 --> 00:39:55.106
<i># As dark as night. #</i>

456
00:39:55.895 --> 00:39:59.615
<i># The sky cries to us all, #</i>

457
00:40:01.190 --> 00:40:05.666
<i># As it sends down its tears. #</i>

458
00:40:06.580 --> 00:40:09.323
<i># Here I stand, #</i>

459
00:40:10.993 --> 00:40:14.681
<i># As she shelters me. #</i>

460
00:40:16.510 --> 00:40:20.607
<i># Distant shadows, #</i>

461
00:40:21.238 --> 00:40:25.181
<i># Mother, please hide. #</i>

462
00:40:26.568 --> 00:40:29.629
<i># They draw so near, #</i>

463
00:40:31.335 --> 00:40:34.928
<i># Oh, these shadows. #</i>

464
00:40:36.788 --> 00:40:40.980
<i># Why are they so close, #</i>

465
00:40:42.303 --> 00:40:46.001
<i># As the sky sends down, #</i>

466
00:40:46.012 --> 00:40:52.580
<i>#  Its tears. #</i>

467
00:41:13.600 --> 00:41:14.800
<i>(distant chatters) Look at him crying!</i>

468
00:41:21.555 --> 00:41:22.936
<i>(distant shouts) Sing one more song!</i>

469
00:42:52.800 --> 00:42:54.510
ABU AL-HAKAM: <i>Blasphemy!</i>

470
00:42:57.380 --> 00:42:58.633
<i> Blasphemy! </i>

471
00:43:06.284 --> 00:43:08.200
Sinners! (whips)

472
00:43:09.088 --> 00:43:10.567
Blasphemers!

473
00:43:10.649 --> 00:43:11.569
GUARD: What are you looking at?

474
00:43:11.612 --> 00:43:12.269
Eyes down, slave!

475
00:43:13.761 --> 00:43:17.850
- You quench your thirst from the 
waters that our Gods has provided you...

476
00:43:20.056 --> 00:43:21.981
...yet what do you offer in return? Huh?

477
00:43:22.034 --> 00:43:24.189
Nothing!

478
00:43:33.092 --> 00:43:36.603
Today you repent to your
sins to me, traitors!

479
00:43:52.526 --> 00:43:53.509
BILAL: No! Soheib!

480
00:43:53.602 --> 00:43:54.983
Let him go!

481
00:43:59.248 --> 00:44:01.079
Cowards!

482
00:44:02.079 --> 00:44:03.079
No!

483
00:44:03.179 --> 00:44:03.984
GUARD: Get this one!

484
00:44:04.993 --> 00:44:05.770
Whip him! (whips)

485
00:44:08.782 --> 00:44:09.908
- <i>Please, stop!</i>

486
00:44:34.334 --> 00:44:35.121
(horse grunts)

487
00:44:38.574 --> 00:44:39.964
GUARD: Please!

488
00:44:47.996 --> 00:44:49.600
PEOPLE: <i> Look, it's him!
- It's the Lion!</i>

489
00:44:50.404 --> 00:44:51.680
PEOPLE: <i>It's the great warrior!
- It is Hamza!</i>

490
00:44:52.842 --> 00:44:54.698
GUARD: Abu Al-Hakam, it's the Lion!

491
00:44:55.708 --> 00:44:57.434
- Hamza! You've arrived just in time.

492
00:44:58.104 --> 00:44:59.453
Look at these dogs!

493
00:44:59.753 --> 00:45:00.424
These sinners!

494
00:45:00.543 --> 00:45:02.424
They must be disciplined and so does... (smacks)

495
00:45:08.065 --> 00:45:09.484
HAMZA: And so does who, coward?

496
00:45:10.839 --> 00:45:12.558
You call yourselves men?

497
00:45:13.203 --> 00:45:16.104
You're a disgrace to Mecca and to
your forefathers! 

498
00:45:16.639 --> 00:45:18.814
Since when were these waters weren't free for all?

499
00:45:19.633 --> 00:45:20.990
And know this,

500
00:45:20.999 --> 00:45:24.017
...I only see God through the actions of men.

501
00:45:27.137 --> 00:45:30.730
Your savagery today uncover
the true color of your belief.

502
00:45:31.203 --> 00:45:32.716
So fight me...!

503
00:45:33.158 --> 00:45:34.987
...or get out of my sight!

504
00:45:37.022 --> 00:45:38.235
AL-SIDDIQ: Hamza!

505
00:45:46.585 --> 00:45:48.256
You arrived just in time, old friend.

506
00:45:49.012 --> 00:45:50.337
- Al-Siddiq! (Abu Bakr)

507
00:45:50.747 --> 00:45:51.440
It has been too long.

508
00:45:51.550 --> 00:45:54.720
- Come, we have much to talk about.

509
00:45:55.124 --> 00:45:57.149
SAAD: Come on Bilal, help me get him up.

509.1
00:45:57.149 --> 00:46:02.149
HAMZA: <i>My people, take as much as you need from 
the Zamzam well, no soldier will stop you.</i>

510
00:46:18.111 --> 00:46:19.991
BILAL: Do you believe change will come?

511
00:46:20.347 --> 00:46:22.397
Even for us?

512
00:46:24.570 --> 00:46:24.888
GHUFAIRA: Maybe.

513
00:46:25.838 --> 00:46:27.956
Mother believed so.

514
00:46:31.956 --> 00:46:34.209
Why are you asking?

515
00:46:37.956 --> 00:46:39.209
Bilal?

516
00:46:43.907 --> 00:46:45.004
- This morning...

517
00:46:47.080 --> 00:46:48.303
...I went to see him again.

518
00:47:02.011 --> 00:47:04.168
AL-SIDDIQ: And who could this be?

519
00:47:04.797 --> 00:47:07.415
There are no young thieves to save
out here.

520
00:47:08.129 --> 00:47:08.993
BILAL: Sir...

521
00:47:09.528 --> 00:47:10.947
...what did you mean before...

522
00:47:11.388 --> 00:47:13.029
...that we choose?

523
00:47:14.351 --> 00:47:15.928
Are you offering to buy me?

524
00:47:19.424 --> 00:47:20.844
- (laughs) Would you like me to?

525
00:47:21.380 --> 00:47:24.985
- Well, you seem like a better master
than the one I serve now.

526
00:47:26.079 --> 00:47:26.994
- Believe it or not, Bilal...

527
00:47:27.655 --> 00:47:29.235
...your master is a slave himself.

528
00:47:30.590 --> 00:47:31.064
- Hmm. Really?

529
00:47:31.694 --> 00:47:33.334
And who is his master?

530
00:47:35.066 --> 00:47:35.572
- Greed...

531
00:47:36.422 --> 00:47:37.558
...the worst of them all.

532
00:47:38.558 --> 00:47:41.656
- Are you saying that no one is ever free?

533
00:47:42.601 --> 00:47:43.737
- I am not.

534
00:47:43.837 --> 00:47:46.229
- And how would I ever be free?

535
00:47:51.773 --> 00:47:54.516
- Only you can enslave yourself, Bilal.

536
00:47:55.240 --> 00:47:56.660
- I-I apologize...

537
00:47:57.478 --> 00:47:58.489
...I just...

538
00:47:58.589 --> 00:48:01.231
...I have never been treated with
such kindness before...

539
00:48:01.499 --> 00:48:03.913
...and I-I still... I don't understand.

540
00:48:04.983 --> 00:48:07.474
Why a noble like you would want...

541
00:48:07.821 --> 00:48:09.108
...to help someone like me?

542
00:48:10.312 --> 00:48:12.866
Is there something you expect me
to do in return?

543
00:48:13.717 --> 00:48:14.411
- You see, Bilal...

544
00:48:15.135 --> 00:48:17.878
...this man (the Prophet Muhammad PBUH)
once guided me when I was truly lost.

545
00:48:18.320 --> 00:48:20.401
A greater noble man...

546
00:48:20.547 --> 00:48:22.892
...who spreads the message of equality.

547
00:48:23.458 --> 00:48:25.476
I have chosen to do the same,

548
00:48:25.792 --> 00:48:27.243
...so here we stand.

549
00:48:27.684 --> 00:48:29.168
And who knows, Bilal...

550
00:48:29.548 --> 00:48:32.797
...perhaps one day , you'll inspire
the hearts of many as well.

551
00:48:33.678 --> 00:48:34.185
- Me?

552
00:48:34.845 --> 00:48:36.108
How can I do that?

553
00:48:36.864 --> 00:48:38.567
- Come, sit.

554
00:48:38.945 --> 00:48:40.900
You sought me out to talk to me,
didn't you?

555
00:48:42.349 --> 00:48:43.107
Let's talk.

556
00:48:49.817 --> 00:48:52.434
GHUFAIRA: So... our mother was right.

557
00:48:53.971 --> 00:48:54.296
BILAL: Yes...

558
00:48:55.776 --> 00:48:56.974
...she was.

559
00:48:57.416 --> 00:48:58.552
- It always seemed that way.

560
00:48:59.433 --> 00:49:01.514
She was always so very wise.

561
00:49:12.067 --> 00:49:14.086
UMAYYA: A toast to my son, Safwan!

562
00:49:14.686 --> 00:49:17.682
He had the business sense to make a killing
on those little idols. <i>(cheers)</i>

563
00:49:20.076 --> 00:49:22.789
Now he can afford
to host his first feast. <i>(cheers)</i>

564
00:49:25.560 --> 00:49:25.879
<i> (toasting) To Safwan! </i>

565
00:49:27.109 --> 00:49:28.426
<i> (chatters) </i>

566
00:49:30.827 --> 00:49:33.759
Are you still sulking because you
passed up a good deal?

567
00:49:34.389 --> 00:49:36.974
I told you these portable idols would sell.

568
00:49:38.328 --> 00:49:41.230
ABU AL-HAKAM: It may be the last money any of us ever make.

569
00:49:42.582 --> 00:49:43.940
- What are you taking about?

570
00:49:44.475 --> 00:49:46.209
There a fortune in these little idols!

571
00:49:46.808 --> 00:49:49.203
Should have heard the priest hawking
them in today the market.

572
00:49:50.936 --> 00:49:52.229
- You were not there later.

573
00:49:52.796 --> 00:49:53.957
There was a dispute...

574
00:49:54.561 --> 00:49:55.760
...and people listened.

575
00:49:57.051 --> 00:49:57.872
- A dispute?

576
00:50:03.197 --> 00:50:04.522
Who created this dispute?

577
00:50:05.498 --> 00:50:07.264
- Wolves, from the new Movement.
(the Prophet Muhammad PBUH)

578
00:50:08.114 --> 00:50:11.298
Their reputation is spreading like 
wildfire across the city!

579
00:50:12.023 --> 00:50:14.891
- Oh, not this business again. If you 
tell me there is an army coming...

580
00:50:15.394 --> 00:50:16.278
...I'll worry.

581
00:50:16.719 --> 00:50:17.919
- What about the talk of freedom?

582
00:50:18.454 --> 00:50:19.558
Do you worry about that?

583 
00:50:20.030 --> 00:50:21.103
- What are you talking about?

584
00:50:21.389 --> 00:50:24.668
- They say we are praying on the people's
desperation.

585
00:50:24.730 --> 00:50:27.976
They say that a real God
would never ask for a man's fortune.

586
00:50:28.764 --> 00:50:30.498
What happens to our business...

587
00:50:30.846 --> 00:50:32.076
...if this message takes hold?

588
00:50:32.458 --> 00:50:35.170
- And how long do you think the other merchants
will tolerate such a message?

589
00:50:36.556 --> 00:50:38.011
They will soon be laughed out of town...

590
00:50:38.359 --> 00:50:40.251
...or someone will strike a deal with them.

591
00:50:41.479 --> 00:50:42.332
You'll see.

592
00:50:47.026 --> 00:50:47.878
Look around!

593
00:50:51.154 --> 00:50:53.173
There is only one God...

594
00:50:53.182 --> 00:50:53.993
...and it is money.

595
00:50:55.569 --> 00:50:58.218
That is the true faith of this city.

596
00:50:59.225 --> 00:51:04.299
- Well these days, not all our 
merchant are worshipping the idols.

597
00:51:04.898 --> 00:51:08.050
- Where is that lazy one
who used to sell idols in sacks?

598
00:51:08.837 --> 00:51:10.949
- He joined the Movement the other day.

599
00:51:12.614 --> 00:51:14.370
- (grunts) And what about the
Lord of Merchants, where is he?

600
00:51:15.199 --> 00:51:17.879
- Oh, joined them too.
A long time ago.

601
00:51:22.824 --> 00:51:24.621
OKBA: Abu Al-Hakam is right.

602
00:51:26.010 --> 00:51:28.312
People still buy my date idols...

603
00:51:28.754 --> 00:51:31.057
..but I think they're eating them for desserts.

604
00:51:37.767 --> 00:51:39.816
- Are there any other traitors in my house?

605
00:51:41.989 --> 00:51:42.622
Well?

606
00:51:44.165 --> 00:51:45.269
Stand, and reveal yourselves!

607
00:51:50.019 --> 00:51:52.107
SAFWAN: Maybe you should ask your slave?

608
00:51:53.033 --> 00:51:54.882
- What? What are you talking about ?

609
00:51:59.096 --> 00:52:00.146
- (sighs) Slave?

610
00:52:01.279 --> 00:52:05.125
Why don't you tell my father
about your new-found friend?

611
00:52:05.386 --> 00:52:06.198
- Impossible!

612
00:52:07.174 --> 00:52:10.295
You must be mistaken.
There are no traitors in my household.

613
00:52:10.429 --> 00:52:11.872
Right, Bilal?

614
00:52:16.250 --> 00:52:16.600
Speak up!

615
00:52:18.049 --> 00:52:19.499
Safwan has accused you something.

616
00:52:20.098 --> 00:52:21.707
What do you have to say for yourself?

617
00:52:22.430 --> 00:52:23.881
I said speak up, slave!

618
00:52:24.638 --> 00:52:27.001
You have my permission to talk!

619
00:52:33.082 --> 00:52:37.683
BILAL: We are - all born equals.

620
00:52:40.172 --> 00:52:41.938
We breathe the same air...

621
00:52:43.954 --> 00:52:45.846
...we bleed the same color...

622
00:52:47.825 --> 00:52:51.519
...and we'll die... and be buried...

623
00:52:51.960 --> 00:52:54.167
...beneath the same ground.

624
00:52:59.807 --> 00:53:04.440
I believe... I am as free a man...

625
00:53:07.023 --> 00:53:08.284
... as you are.

626
00:53:09.404 --> 00:53:11.755
- Free? Equal?

627
00:53:12.196 --> 00:53:13.459
I hate these words.

628
00:53:14.216 --> 00:53:17.715
Umayya, this one woke up on the wrong side
of the ground today. (chuckles)

629
00:53:18.376 --> 00:53:20.433
Free? Equals huh?

630
00:53:20.993 --> 00:53:22.444
Everyone! Look here!

631
00:53:22.948 --> 00:53:26.005
We are both equals!

632
00:53:28.304 --> 00:53:31.300
- You once slapped my face because I let this slave
make a fool of you.

633
00:53:31.834 --> 00:53:34.380
What are you going to do now, Father?

634
00:53:41.081 --> 00:53:43.907
- Guards!

635
00:53:53.011 --> 00:53:58.274
MOTHER: <i>*Being a great man begins with 
taking off your chains.*</i>

636
00:54:14.360 --> 00:54:15.316
GUARD: <i>Quickly slave, move it!</i>

637
00:54:15.928 --> 00:54:17.372
<i>(door slams)</i>

638
00:54:18.039 --> 00:54:21.000
Bind him! Renounce your claim!

639
00:54:21.202 --> 00:54:22.551
Renounce!

640
00:54:23.708 --> 00:54:24.590
UMAYYA: <i>Crush his spirit.</i>

641
00:54:25.103 --> 00:54:27.978
<i>Let him rot inside the cage.</i>

642
00:54:29.283 --> 00:54:30.156
<i>No water...</i>

643
00:54:30.296 --> 00:54:32.182
<i>...no food.</i>

644
00:54:32.183 --> 00:54:33.677
<i>He'll come back.</i>

645
00:54:34.842 --> 00:54:35.840
SAAD: <i>Bilal, hang in there...</i>

646
00:54:36.000 --> 00:54:36.800
<i>...I will bring help.</i>

647
00:54:37.797 --> 00:54:42.001
MOTHER: <i>*I see the heart of a great man, Bilal.*</i>

648
00:54:42.021 --> 00:54:43.055
GUARD: <i>Renounce your claim!</i>

649
00:54:45.452 --> 00:54:48.315
<i>No one is to touch this slave! Umayya's orders!</i>

650
00:54:48.715 --> 00:54:49.801
<i>Renounce your claim, slave! </i>

651
00:54:50.212 --> 00:54:51.349
BILAL: I will not!

652
00:54:52.517 --> 00:54:53.497
(screams)

653
00:54:54.727 --> 00:54:56.250
GHUFAIRA: <i>Bilal, are you alright?</i>

654
00:54:56.290 --> 00:54:57.512
SAAD: <i>You have to be strong, Bilal.</i>

655
00:54:57.922 --> 00:54:59.969
SAFWAN: <i>A master breeds a master...</i>

656
00:55:00.912 --> 00:55:03.689
<i>...and a slave breeds a slave.</i>

657
00:55:09.231 --> 00:55:11.668
AS-SIDDIQ: <i>*All humanity is a single nation...*</i>

658
00:55:11.723 --> 00:55:13.116
GHUFAIRA: <i>Bilal, are you alright?</i>

659
00:55:13.296 --> 00:55:15.781
<i>*...for those who look outside...*</i>

660
00:55:15.981 --> 00:55:17.649
<i>*...only dream.*</i>

661
00:55:22.351 --> 00:55:23.946
MOTHER: <i>*Guidance will come, you'll see.*</i>

662
00:55:32.348 --> 00:55:35.637
UMAYYA: <i>And what is the difference
between you and this apple?</i>

663
00:55:36.015 --> 00:55:37.000
<i>(whispers) Renounce your claim...</i>

664
00:55:40.073 --> 00:55:42.304
SAFWAN: <i>Kneel when you come before me, slave!</i>

665
00:55:42.546 --> 00:55:46.977
AL-SIDDIQ: <i>*And those who look within...
are awakened.*</i>

666
00:56:05.809 --> 00:56:07.809
<i>*When you are awakened...*</i>

667
00:56:07.809 --> 00:56:10.144
<i>*...your story will race out of this desert...*</i>

668
00:56:10.344 --> 00:56:13.503
<i>*...across the world...*</i>

669
00:56:18.236 --> 00:56:21.826
<i>*...where great men are tested.* </i>

670
00:56:35.667 --> 00:56:37.720
<i>*Prepare yourself, Bilal.*</i>

671
00:56:38.120 --> 00:56:42.667
MOTHER: <i>*Being a great man...
means living without chains.*</i>

672
00:57:27.626 --> 00:57:30.079
UMAYYA: Bilal, are you awake?

673
00:57:32.172 --> 00:57:34.311
Good.

674
00:57:35.110 --> 00:57:37.178
You're braver than I thought.

675
00:57:39.197 --> 00:57:41.087
I take credit for that.

676
00:57:42.343 --> 00:57:45.351
It comes from watching me all these
years, I'm sure.

677
00:57:45.751 --> 00:57:47.150
<i> (whispers) Why don't you just die?</i>

678
00:57:47.450 --> 00:57:50.122
It took guts to reveal yourself like that...

679
00:57:50.238 --> 00:57:54.642
...but sadly, you still think like a slave.

680
00:58:00.015 --> 00:58:03.110
I'll get you back on track
with a little secret. See...

681
00:58:03.992 --> 00:58:06.202
...I never believed in these Gods.

682
00:58:06.602 --> 00:58:08.907
No, no, no, no. I'm not a fool.

683
00:58:12.399 --> 00:58:15.203
The truth is... we are both slaves, Bilal.

684
00:58:15.403 --> 00:58:17.029
The difference between us...

685
00:58:17.881 --> 00:58:20.375
...is I worship whatever empowers me.

686
00:58:21.772 --> 00:58:23.603
You...

687
00:58:24.386 --> 00:58:28.102
...worship something that will destroy you.

688
00:58:37.428 --> 00:58:41.773
A free man would have sought out the profit
in this situation.

689
00:58:41.845 --> 00:58:47.123
For example a free man might offer 
to spy on his master's enemies.

690
00:58:47.123 --> 00:58:50.095
He might realize the advantage in that.

691
00:58:50.195 --> 00:58:53.757
Do you understand what I'm saying, Bilal ?

692
00:58:55.438 --> 00:58:57.122
Get him some water.

693
00:59:05.503 --> 00:59:08.267
Should i take off these chains?

694
00:59:10.438 --> 00:59:12.180
What do you say, Bilal?

695
00:59:12.574 --> 00:59:15.095
- My chains...

696
00:59:15.131 --> 00:59:17.246
...are already off.

697
00:59:17.351 --> 00:59:18.146
- That's funny...

698
00:59:18.247 --> 00:59:20.484
...because I see them.

699
00:59:21.036 --> 00:59:25.097
Or does your invisible God make other 
things invisible too?

700
00:59:25.102 --> 00:59:28.002
- I'm talking about the chains...

701
00:59:28.601 --> 00:59:29.379
...in here.

702
00:59:29.379 --> 00:59:31.012
- Stop talking in riddles!

703
00:59:31.612 --> 00:59:34.105
Do you know how much trouble you're in?

704
00:59:34.205 --> 00:59:35.567
I can have you killed right now.

705
00:59:36.567 --> 00:59:39.968
- It doesn't matter what you do to me...

706
00:59:40.168 --> 00:59:44.449
...and there's nothing you can give me.

707
00:59:46.466 --> 00:59:50.123
I am... already free.

708
00:59:50.123 --> 00:59:52.096
- And what about your sister?

709
00:59:52.096 --> 00:59:54.191
Is she free too?

710
00:59:55.122 --> 00:59:57.410
So, are you going to consider my 
proposition or not?

711
00:59:59.210 --> 01:00:00.604
You wanted a horse?

712
01:00:01.287 --> 01:00:02.204
I will give you two.

713
01:00:02.497 --> 01:00:06.012
And I will provide both you and your 
sister, a home.

714
01:00:06.123 --> 01:00:07.808
<i>(whispers) Accept his offer!</i>

715
01:00:12.119 --> 01:00:15.000
<i>(shouts outside) Bring him out here! Bring him!
- Bring him out!</i>

716
01:00:17.514 --> 01:00:18.905
<i>(shouts outside) Let him go!</i>

717
01:00:19.106 --> 01:00:22.306
- This is why you are a slave while I am rich!

718
01:00:23.030 --> 01:00:26.304
You don't recognize when you've 
been given an opportunity.

719
01:00:26.530 --> 01:00:28.104
Too bad.

720
01:00:28.404 --> 01:00:29.544
- Then, kill me.

721
01:00:29.985 --> 01:00:31.918
- I'm not going to kill you.

722
01:00:34.899 --> 01:00:37.730
Yet, you might still die.

723
01:00:52.138 --> 01:00:53.454
GUARD: Your time has come.

724
01:01:25.517 --> 01:01:26.867
SAAD: No, Bilal!

725
01:01:28.539 --> 01:01:30.576
CHARLATAN PRIEST: Tell me, slave.
Who are you going to?

726
01:01:30.601 --> 01:01:33.544
Is He stronger than I am?

727
01:01:33.741 --> 01:01:36.595
Is He stronger than my Gods?

728
01:01:36.695 --> 01:01:38.182
For with their power...

729
01:01:38.224 --> 01:01:39.171
...and mine...

730
01:01:39.271 --> 01:01:40.420
...I can have you killed...

731
01:01:40.537 --> 01:01:42.022
...or set free.

732
01:01:42.655 --> 01:01:43.729
This....

733
01:01:44.518 --> 01:01:46.079
...is my God.

734
01:01:46.300 --> 01:01:49.100
Do you want it to come to your aid?

735
01:01:49.241 --> 01:01:50.463
Accept...

736
01:01:50.496 --> 01:01:53.894
...and I will ask it to absolve you
of your sins.

737
01:01:54.103 --> 01:01:55.775
AS-SIDDIQ: I've already offered a fair price for him.

738
01:01:56.969 --> 01:01:58.296
UMAYYA: Very fair.

739
01:01:58.996 --> 01:02:01.481
- Then what is the reason for bringing him out here?

740
01:02:06.696 --> 01:02:08.297
<i> (shouts) Crush him! </i>

741
01:02:28.082 --> 01:02:29.004
- If you injure him...

742
01:02:29.122 --> 01:02:31.710
...then he is of no value to me...

743
01:02:31.990 --> 01:02:33.384
...and the deal is off.

744
01:02:33.711 --> 01:02:35.648
- We'll see.

745
01:02:35.942 --> 01:02:38.386
CHARLATAN PRIEST: This slave
has been charged with the most heinous of crimes!

746
01:02:41.148 --> 01:02:43.280
He stands against his masters!

747
01:02:44.068 --> 01:02:47.209
For this offense...

748
01:02:47.557 --> 01:02:48.747
...he will be punished!

749
01:03:01.210 --> 01:03:02.654
GHUFAIRA: No!

750
01:03:03.261 --> 01:03:04.269
<i>You will kill him!</i>

751
01:03:06.000 --> 01:03:08.441
<i>Please! No! Stop!</i>

752
01:03:10.744 --> 01:03:11.000
(grunts)

753
01:03:16.434 --> 01:03:18.447
GHUFAIRA:<i> He will die, Safwan!</i>

754
01:03:18.935 --> 01:03:19.647
<i> Please, no! </i>

755
01:03:20.467 --> 01:03:21.849
SAFWAN: Feel that...

756
01:03:21.953 --> 01:03:22.673
...slave?

757
01:03:22.674 --> 01:03:25.125
Give up, Bilal.

758
01:03:26.969 --> 01:03:28.032
You can end this.

759
01:03:28.126 --> 01:03:30.415
Cry for forgiveness...

760
01:03:30.926 --> 01:03:33.515
...and accept us as your real masters.

761
01:03:34.083 --> 01:03:34.924
And these....

762
01:03:35.556 --> 01:03:36.639
...as your true Gods!

763
01:03:38.374 --> 01:03:40.111
How many Gods are there?

764
01:03:40.511 --> 01:03:41.095
Can you count...

765
01:03:41.131 --> 01:03:42.670
...slave?

766
01:03:53.163 --> 01:03:55.100
- One...

767
01:03:55.141 --> 01:03:57.091
...only One!

768
01:04:14.094 --> 01:04:15.295
CHARLATAN PRIEST: It can't be!

769
01:04:16.071 --> 01:04:18.025
SAFWAN: You are a fool!

770
01:04:19.124 --> 01:04:20.513
BILAL: I... am...

771
01:04:22.017 --> 01:04:24.029
...free.

772
01:04:30.063 --> 01:04:31.200
GHUFAIRA: No, no, Bilal!

773
01:04:31.178 --> 01:04:33.465
<i>Please, stop!</i>

774
01:04:33.471 --> 01:04:34.383
<i>He will die!</i>

775
01:04:34.582 --> 01:04:35.456
AL-SIDDIQ: I will double the offer.

776
01:04:36.151 --> 01:04:38.287
UMAYYA: I think you've lost your head for business.

777
01:04:40.833 --> 01:04:42.412
Sold!

778
01:04:42.494 --> 01:04:44.316
Remove the stone.

779
01:04:54.357 --> 01:04:55.746
SAAD: Bilal?

780
01:04:56.330 --> 01:04:59.335
- I would've given all I own for him.

781
01:05:01.044 --> 01:05:02.144
- For a slave?

782
01:05:02.595 --> 01:05:03.291
- No.

783
01:05:05.396 --> 01:05:06.692
For a brother.

784
01:05:07.890 --> 01:05:10.064
- Don't tell me that this new Movement...

785
01:05:10.086 --> 01:05:12.644
...makes slaves and nobles brothers!

786
01:05:18.385 --> 01:05:19.842
- It does.

787
01:05:25.960 --> 01:05:26.251
SAAD: Easy, easy.

788
01:05:27.238 --> 01:05:28.596
- Bilal? Talk to me.

789
01:05:30.420 --> 01:05:31.588
- His sister!

790
01:05:32.196 --> 01:05:34.333
I'll pay the same for her!

791
01:05:34.937 --> 01:05:36.401
- You're asking the wrong person.

792
01:05:36.401 --> 01:05:39.446
I gave it to Safwan as a gift.

793
01:05:41.948 --> 01:05:42.960
SAFWAN: I won't sell her...

794
01:05:43.460 --> 01:05:47.063
...not even for your whole business.

795
01:05:47.163 --> 01:05:48.020
Take her!

796
01:05:48.027 --> 01:05:48.118
GHUFAIRA: No!

797
01:05:48.119 --> 01:05:50.019
AL-SIDDIQ: What is the meaning of this?

798
01:05:50.119 --> 01:05:51.319
Unhand her!

799
01:05:52.119 --> 01:05:53.319
- Bilal!

799.1
01:05:54.119 --> 01:05:56.319
BILAL: Ghufaira!

800
01:06:10.998 --> 01:06:14.988
Three months later...

801
01:06:15.995 --> 01:06:19.031
BILAL: <i>I will forever be grateful...</i>

802
01:06:19.131 --> 01:06:20.971
<i>...for you have saved my life.</i>

803
01:06:22.038 --> 01:06:24.389
AL-SIDDIQ: <i>To save one life, my brother...</i>

804
01:06:24.438 --> 01:06:27.535
<i>...is like saving all humanity.</i>

805
01:06:29.298 --> 01:06:31.250
SAAD: So how does it feel to walk the
streets of Mecca...

806
01:06:31.341 --> 01:06:33.607
...as a free man?

807
01:06:34.529 --> 01:06:36.704
- (sighs) It feels good just to be walking.

808
01:06:37.554 --> 01:06:38.809
Where's Soheib?

809
01:06:38.945 --> 01:06:39.866
- With Hamza...

810
01:06:39.922 --> 01:06:41.247
...and the Lord of Merchants (Al-Siddiq).

811
01:06:41.222 --> 01:06:43.247
They wait for us at the gate.

812
01:06:47.364 --> 01:06:49.980
AL-SIDDIQ: <i>Word of your defiance makes its
way through all the city.</i>

813
01:06:49.990 --> 01:06:52.742
<i>Umayya and the slave masters 
will come for you...</i>

814
01:06:52.812 --> 01:06:53.697
<i>...Bilal.</i>

815
01:06:54.295 --> 01:06:55.696
<i>We must leave.</i>

816
01:06:55.686 --> 01:06:57.326
<i>- Where would we go?</i>

817
01:06:57.925 --> 01:06:59.915
<i>To a great city.</i>

818
01:06:59.995 --> 01:07:02.916
<i>One that welcomes us with open hearts.</i>

819
01:07:53.999 --> 01:07:55.474
HAMZA: Attractive, isn't it?

820
01:07:57.017 --> 01:07:59.252
Men crafted the blade to hunt and...

821
01:07:59.817 --> 01:08:01.207
...provide food for his family.

822
01:08:01.836 --> 01:08:03.131
These days...

823
01:08:03.698 --> 01:08:04.980
...men use it...

824
01:08:04.990 --> 01:08:07.295
...to break each other.

825
01:08:07.395 --> 01:08:08.841
Its true purpose and value...

826
01:08:10.001 --> 01:08:11.052
...has been lost.

827
01:08:11.869 --> 01:08:12.938
BILAL: Will you teach me how to fight?

828
01:08:13.446 --> 01:08:15.119
- Why?

829
01:08:15.684 --> 01:08:17.454
You think if you have wielded a weapon...

830
01:08:17.654 --> 01:08:20.138
...the outcome might've been in your favor...

831
01:08:20.492 --> 01:08:24.030
...or do you seek to take what you desire,
with the sword?

832
01:08:28.035 --> 01:08:29.324
Remember...

833
01:08:29.750 --> 01:08:32.605
...I can only show you how to use it...

834
01:08:32.653 --> 01:08:34.285
...but you alone must decide...

835
01:08:34.347 --> 01:08:35.544
...where and when.

836
01:08:38.196 --> 01:08:40.976
Violence does not always solve disputes.

837
01:08:41.539 --> 01:08:44.624
Do not allow yourself to be lured into a battle...

838
01:08:44.717 --> 01:08:46.579
...you can avoid.

839
01:08:53.074 --> 01:08:55.141
- When do we start?

840
01:08:55.706 --> 01:08:57.190
- As soon as you put back the
sword...

841
01:08:57.290 --> 01:08:59.190
...and pick up that stick.

842
01:10:02.867 --> 01:10:04.099
HAMZA: Saad!

843
01:10:09.414 --> 01:10:10.896
Alright.

844
01:10:11.526 --> 01:10:12.410
Let's try some sparring.

845
01:10:13.137 --> 01:10:14.312
SAAD: Show me what you've got, rookie.

846
01:10:14.683 --> 01:10:17.158
BILAL: Ha! After you 'apple-hunter'.

847
01:10:20.051 --> 01:10:21.138
HAMZA: Turn around!

848
01:10:21.804 --> 01:10:22.800
Duck!

849
01:10:23.000 --> 01:10:23.900
Now parry!

850
01:10:24.000 --> 01:10:25.755
<i>As we practiced, Bilal.
As we practiced!</i>

851
01:10:31.900 --> 01:10:33.100
<i> My, you're not bad Bilal.</i>

852
01:10:35.417 --> 01:10:37.080
<i> Try to dodge this!</i>

853
01:11:05.446 --> 01:11:07.827
BILAL: Ghufaira?

854
01:12:28.100 --> 01:12:30.280
SAAD: Ha! I beat you again.

855
01:12:31.700 --> 01:12:33.500
Come, get up.

856
01:12:35.800 --> 01:12:37.700
Let's spar when you cool down, Bilal.

857
01:12:40.000 --> 01:12:42.152
AL-SIDDIQ: Never stike in anger.

858
01:12:43.813 --> 01:12:45.169
We will free her, Bilal.

859
01:12:45.170 --> 01:12:47.170
Do not lose hope.

860
01:12:52.234 --> 01:12:56.465
He who conquers his anger is strong...

861
01:12:56.465 --> 01:13:00.177
...he who forgives when having the power
to seek revenge...

862
01:13:00.177 --> 01:13:01.730
...will witness glory.

863
01:13:01.875 --> 01:13:02.853
- I promise...

864
01:13:03.452 --> 01:13:05.029
...I will try harder.

865
01:13:05.129 --> 01:13:08.378
- Promise me to train this.

866
01:13:08.986 --> 01:13:12.026
True strength is in the mind, Bilal.
Not in the weapon.

867
01:13:12.152 --> 01:13:13.982
And thats is Hamza's secret.

868
01:13:14.738 --> 01:13:16.581
One day...

869
01:13:16.781 --> 01:13:17.700
...you'll discover your own secret.

870
01:13:22.038 --> 01:13:26.000
<i># The full moon rose over us, #</i>

871
01:13:26.070 --> 01:13:28.370
<i># From the valley of Wada'; #</i>

872
01:13:29.367 --> 01:13:33.058
<i># And it is incumbent upon us to show gratitude, #</i>

873
01:13:33.059 --> 01:13:36.926
<i># For as long as anyone in existence calls out to Allah. #</i>

874
01:13:36.927 --> 01:13:37.927
(horses neigh)

875
01:13:48.728 --> 01:13:49.728
Hiyaah!

876
01:13:51.915 --> 01:13:56.122
<i># Oh our Messenger amongst us, #</i>

877
01:13:56.215 --> 01:13:59.412
<i># Who comes with the exhortations to be heeded; #</i>

878
01:13:59.512 --> 01:14:04.231
<i># You have brought to this city nobility, #</i>

879
01:14:04.351 --> 01:14:09.172
<i># Welcome oh you who call us to a good way. #</i>

880
01:14:09.272 --> 01:14:15.072
<i># Welcome oh you who call us to a good way. #</i>

881
01:14:15.273 --> 01:14:15.313


882
01:14:15.400 --> 01:14:15.777


883
01:14:16.150 --> 01:14:18.200
<i> (children shouts) </i>

884
01:14:18.950 --> 01:14:21.300
<i> (children laughs) </i>

885
01:14:21.850 --> 01:14:23.868
(girl grunts & sighs)

886
01:14:25.224 --> 01:14:28.074
GIRL: Come with me,
we wil take you to your home!

887
01:14:32.125 --> 01:14:34.674
BILAL: (laughs) Wait, where we are going?

888
01:14:35.825 --> 01:14:36.274
<i>(child shouts) Bilal!</i>

889
01:14:40.856 --> 01:14:41.805
<i>Where are you taking me?</i>

890
01:15:11.543 --> 01:15:13.000
BILAL: <i>Mother!</i>

891
01:15:13.290 --> 01:15:14.500
<i>Watch me build the home.</i>

892
01:15:27.555 --> 01:15:30.000
BILAL: <i>Watch us build a house...</i>

893
01:15:30.001 --> 01:15:32.012
<i>...where we can gather...</i>

894
01:15:32.013 --> 01:15:33.621
<i>...to spread hope.</i>

895
01:15:33.731 --> 01:15:34.555
<i>Hope...</i>

896
01:15:34.556 --> 01:15:37.616
<i>...to inspire the hearts of men.</i>

897
01:15:52.201 --> 01:15:55.550
AL-SIDDIQ: He (Muhammad) asks,
that you call out to them...

898
01:15:55.550 --> 01:15:57.050
...Master Bilal.

899
01:16:06.900 --> 01:16:08.206
BILAL: <i>From here...</i>

900
01:16:09.276 --> 01:16:11.380
<i>...I will call them.</i>

901
01:16:17.221 --> 01:16:18.257
MOTHER: <i>Show me.</i>

902
01:16:20.521 --> 01:16:23.200
<i>Show me how your voice
will inspire.</i>

903
01:16:24.152 --> 01:16:29.240


904
01:16:25.000 --> 01:16:28.000
<i>How it will be raised to speak 
for justice...</i>

905
01:16:29.348 --> 01:16:30.100
<i>...and equality.</i>

906
01:16:37.242 --> 01:16:39.971
ABU AL-HAKAM: What I feared
is happening, Umayya.

907
01:16:39.991 --> 01:16:43.073
They're growing in strength
and numbers.

908
01:16:43.243 --> 01:16:46.017
Are we to stand here, and do nothing?

909
01:16:46.018 --> 01:16:48.507
SAFWAN: He is right, Father.

910
01:16:48.887 --> 01:16:50.684
When a slave defies his master...

911
01:16:50.984 --> 01:16:52.828
...the world turns upside down!

912
01:16:52.928 --> 01:16:57.900
<i>(whispers) Kill them!
Kill them all!</i>

913
01:16:58.812 --> 01:16:59.193
<i>(whispers) Kill!</i>

914
01:17:05.185 --> 01:17:06.920
UMAYYA: We will begin here...

915
01:17:07.123 --> 01:17:09.253
...tonight!

916 
01:17:09.254 --> 01:17:11.200
Assemble a great army to crush each...

917
01:17:11.280 --> 01:17:15.026
...and every place that shelters them.

918
01:17:15.694 --> 01:17:19.026
Let it start at with our own households.

919
01:17:19.125 --> 01:17:21.236
Root them all out...

920
01:17:22.525 --> 01:17:23.836
...and kill them.

921
01:17:26.983 --> 01:17:28.895
<i>(whispers) Kill them all!</i>

922
01:17:33.450 --> 01:17:37.987
<i>(shouts) Open the gate!
- Hamza is back with more refugees!</i>

923
01:17:54.803 --> 01:17:56.348
HAMZA: Magnificent horse.

924
01:17:56.979 --> 01:17:58.485
It followed us on the way back.

925
01:17:58.885 --> 01:17:59.402
Do you know him?

926
01:17:59.981 --> 01:18:01.054
BILAL: I do.

927
01:18:01.995 --> 01:18:03.000
We are old friends. (clicks)

928
01:18:06.183 --> 01:18:08.591
He was once owned by Umayya.

929
01:18:08.691 --> 01:18:11.239
- Hmm. Seems he has escaped his oppression
as well.

930
01:18:11.439 --> 01:18:13.440
Take good care of him.

931
01:18:16.795 --> 01:18:18.493
<i>(man shouts) The old man bring news
from Mecca!</i>

932
01:18:19.314 --> 01:18:20.797
OLD MAN: The persecution...

933
01:18:21.047 --> 01:18:22.783
...grows worse every day.

934
01:18:23.287 --> 01:18:24.678
We've lost so much...

935
01:18:25.247 --> 01:18:26.163
...but we were lucky.

936
01:18:26.541 --> 01:18:28.182
We have escaped!

937
01:18:28.445 --> 01:18:29.982
The ones who remain...

938
01:18:30.749 --> 01:18:33.413
...I fear may soon lose their life.

939
01:18:33.913 --> 01:18:35.737
SOLDIER: A message for you,
from the son Umayya.

940
01:18:46.012 --> 01:18:47.386
BILAL: Ghufaira!

941
01:18:48.031 --> 01:18:49.555
AL-SIDDIQ: Where is Bilal?

942
01:18:49.731 --> 01:18:50.555
HAMZA: He's over there, brother.

943
01:20:09.174 --> 01:20:11.249
MAN: My child!

944
01:20:11.847 --> 01:20:13.300
HAMZA: Where are the rest of you?

945
01:20:14.047 --> 01:20:15.300
- We are the only ones left.

946
01:20:18.059 --> 01:20:18.407
BILAL: <i>Hiyahh!</i>

947
01:20:44.419 --> 01:20:45.737
BILAL: Ghufaira!

948
01:20:47.654 --> 01:20:48.632
Ghufaira!

949
01:20:49.546 --> 01:20:50.430
GUARD: Take him outside!

950
01:20:50.430 --> 01:20:51.430
Follow me!

951
01:20:53.834 --> 01:20:55.000
SLAVE: <i>Please, have mercy!</i>

952
01:20:57.134 --> 01:20:58.145
SOLDIER: The slave! Get him!

953
01:21:09.123 --> 01:21:10.424
- Got him!

954
01:21:10.924 --> 01:21:12.960
SOLDIER: You made a great mistake
coming back here, boy!

955
01:21:13.260 --> 01:21:14.116
- Get him up!

956
01:21:16.300 --> 01:21:18.193
- Where is your God now?

957
01:21:23.519 --> 01:21:24.993
SAFWAN: Wait!

958
01:21:45.519 --> 01:21:46.093
BILAL: Ghufaira...

959
01:21:46.119 --> 01:21:47.993
SAFWAN: Proceed.

960
01:21:53.519 --> 01:21:55.993
SOLDIER: Time to meet your God!

961
01:22:10.119 --> 01:22:11.119
HAMZA: Come!

962
01:22:20.559 --> 01:22:22.119
I am not leaving without you.

963
01:22:22.519 --> 01:22:23.119
Hurry!

964
01:22:24.419 --> 01:22:26.119
<i> (guards shout)</i>

965
01:22:40.419 --> 01:22:41.119
<i>(guard shouts)</i>

966
01:22:42.419 --> 01:22:43.119


967
01:23:05.679 --> 01:23:06.967
One year later...

968
01:23:36.968 --> 01:23:40.968
HAMZA: I knew I would find you here.

969
01:23:43.467 --> 01:23:46.811
I have no words
that can make you feel better.

970
01:23:48.576 --> 01:23:50.877
I can only ask you to
keep your mind clear...

971
01:23:51.381 --> 01:23:52.927
...and your heart, true.

972
01:23:54.376 --> 01:23:55.606
And rest assured...

973
01:23:55.923 --> 01:23:57.879
...God will always be there for 
you, Bilal.

974
01:24:01.534 --> 01:24:03.520
I have made this for you.

975
01:24:23.468 --> 01:24:24.761
When you decide to use it...

976
01:24:25.266 --> 01:24:26.065
...remember...

977
01:24:26.066 --> 01:24:30.155
...not to allow the blade
to dictate your choices.

978
01:24:37.403 --> 01:24:38.416
AL-SIDDIQ: <i>*O Lord...*</i>

979
01:24:38.858 --> 01:24:40.687
<i>*All praise and glory belong to you.*</i>

980
01:24:41.726 --> 01:24:43.398
<i>*Upon you we rely...*</i>

981
01:24:44.595 --> 01:24:47.874
<i>*...in both hardship and ease.*</i>

982
01:25:03.629 --> 01:25:05.868
UMAYYA: These fools band together to 
overthrow us.


983
01:25:06.435 --> 01:25:07.886
I will lead the attack at the front.

984
01:25:08.831 --> 01:25:10.315
You must watch over the city.

985
01:25:14.473 --> 01:25:15.833
They threaten our control...

986
01:25:16.400 --> 01:25:17.032
...our power.

987
01:25:17.788 --> 01:25:19.806
Do not disappoint me.

988
01:25:34.868 --> 01:25:36.792
AL-SIDDIQ: <i>*Protect us from all evil...*</i>

989
01:25:39.628 --> 01:25:44.261
<i>*...for there is no might,*
*...nor power, except with You.*</i>

990
01:25:45.018 --> 01:25:45.743
<i>(altogether) Amen!</i>

991
01:26:12.687 --> 01:26:13.887
UMAYYA: You must be joking.

992
01:26:22.205 --> 01:26:23.625
ABU AL-HAKAM: Most unfortunate.

993
01:26:34.000 --> 01:26:35.860
SOLDIERS: <i>Look at their strength!
- They are too many!</i>

994
01:26:36.064 --> 01:26:37.840
HAMZA: Stand strong, men!

995
01:26:39.063 --> 01:26:40.000
Have faith.

996
01:26:43.325 --> 01:26:44.934
UMAYYA: Send three of our best here.

997
01:26:45.474 --> 01:26:46.892
First, we destroy their morale...

998
01:26:47.837 --> 01:26:48.973
...then we finish them...

999
01:26:49.603 --> 01:26:50.424
...one by one.

1000
01:26:54.898 --> 01:26:57.138
HAMZA: Whatever happens, don't come for us.

1001
01:26:57.139 --> 01:26:58.139
Stand your ground!

1002
01:27:06.118 --> 01:27:07.317
SOLDIER: <i>Make way!</i>

1003
01:27:07.760 --> 01:27:10.000
<i>Make way for Ali!
- Make way for Ali!</i>

1004
01:27:09.897 --> 01:27:11.897


1005
01:27:30.671 --> 01:27:32.690
UMAYYA: I'm going to enjoy this!
(Okba laughs)

1006
01:27:34.671 --> 01:27:36.690
<i>(shouts) Take them down!

1007
01:29:20.484 --> 01:29:22.129
UMAYYA: Charge!

1008
01:29:22.746 --> 01:29:23.000
- Slay them all!

1009
01:29:29.132 --> 01:29:30.426
BILAL: Come on, Hamza!
Move!

1010
01:29:41.029 --> 01:29:42.190
HAMZA: Archers!

1011
01:29:42.199 --> 01:29:43.190
SAAD: Archers!

1012
01:29:43.191 --> 01:29:44.191
BILAL: No!

1013
01:29:45.001 --> 01:29:46.531
- Always trust the Lion.

1014
01:29:46.532 --> 01:29:47.532
HAMZA: Fire!

1015
01:29:47.533 --> 01:29:48.533
SAAD: Fire!

1016
01:29:55.769 --> 01:29:56.621
SOLDIER: Fire!

1017
01:31:56.593 --> 01:31:58.605
SOHEIB: (laughs) Yes!

1018
01:32:36.019 --> 01:32:37.564
HAMZA: (chuckles) Where did that come from?

1019
01:32:38.559 --> 01:32:40.894
BILAL: I learnt.
From the best.

1020
01:33:59.171 --> 01:34:00.086
UMAYYA: Slave!

1021
01:34:49.621 --> 01:34:50.662
BILAL: We are brothers...

1022
01:34:50.980 --> 01:34:51.612
...killing brothers!

1023
01:34:52.966 --> 01:34:54.732
Put an end to this!

1024
01:34:55.299 --> 01:34:56.435
Be the better man.

1025
01:34:57.835 --> 01:34:59.734
UMAYYA: (laughs)
You're not my brother, boy!

1026
01:35:01.000 --> 01:35:02.234
Show me what you've got!

1027
01:35:03.000 --> 01:35:05.000
This is how you treat your master?

1028
01:35:05.524 --> 01:35:07.039
Let this be the day...

1029
01:35:07.637 --> 01:35:09.027
...I finally put you out of your misery!

1030
01:35:10.161 --> 01:35:10.998
- Not today...

1031
01:35:11.975 --> 01:35:12.943
...Umayya!

1032
01:35:37.406 --> 01:35:41.038
UMAYYA: It's time...
for you to join your sister!

1033
01:36:18.732 --> 01:36:20.088
(shouts) <i>The ruler of Mecca has fallen!</i>

1034 
01:36:20.561 --> 01:36:21.540
<i>- Umayya is no more!</i>

1035
01:36:22.335 --> 01:36:26.232
<i>- Send word to the rulers in all of Hijaz!
We must prepare for battle!</i>

1036
01:36:27.670 --> 01:36:29.461
<i>- Get Master Safwan!
After them all!</i>

1037
01:36:29.509 --> 01:36:31.402
<i> (shouts outside) </i>

1038
01:36:32.442 --> 01:36:33.420


1039
01:36:57.525 --> 01:36:59.546
AL-SIDDIQ: <i> *There will be victories.*</i>

1040
01:37:01.407 --> 01:37:02.667
<i> *Victories of the mind...*</i>

1041
01:37:03.770 --> 01:37:04.496
<i> *...and of the soul.*</i>

1042
01:37:06.765 --> 01:37:09.413
<i> * Victories that break the chains...*</i>

1043
01:37:10.044 --> 01:37:12.251
<i> *...which bind mankind.*</i>

1044
01:37:13.000 --> 01:37:14.718
HAMZA: You did well, little brother.

1045
01:37:20.133 --> 01:37:22.909
Al-SIDDIQ: <i> *Victories that unite us as one.*</i>

1046
01:37:28.793 --> 01:37:33.284
<i> *Yet this enemy will not surrender.*</i>

1047
01:37:52.120 --> 01:37:53.035
<i> *It will plan...*</i>

1048
01:37:54.642 --> 01:37:56.755
<i> *...it will linger in the darkness...*</i>
(whispers) Kill him...

1049
01:38:00.788 --> 01:38:02.208
<i> *...waiting for the opportunity...*</i>

1050
01:38:02.901 --> 01:38:04.383
<i> *...to strike for our heart.*</i>

1051 
01:38:16.829 --> 01:38:19.006
<i> *There will be victories...*</i>

1052
01:39:08.791 --> 01:39:11.534
<i> *...and there will be losses...*</i>

1053
01:39:12.321 --> 01:39:14.057
<i> *...that break our hearts.*</i>

1054
01:39:23.667 --> 01:39:24.897
<i> *Hate not, my brothers...*</i>

1055
01:39:26.756 --> 01:39:28.365
<i> *...for hate...*</i>

1056
01:39:28.776 --> 01:39:29.691
<i> *...is a terrible thing.*</i>

1057
01:39:32.401 --> 01:39:34.801
<i> *War awaits us.*</i>

1058
01:39:36.974 --> 01:39:38.961
<i> *May the Light prevail.*</i>

1059
01:40:03.578 --> 01:40:04.897
MECCA

1060
01:41:12.077 --> 01:41:14.663
SAFWAN: Is this how you express your faith, Bilal?

1061
01:41:18.412 --> 01:41:19.517
Be finished with this.

1062
01:41:35.177 --> 01:41:35.998
BILAL: Why?

1063
01:41:37.543 --> 01:41:39.782
Why did you kill her?

1064
01:41:41.641 --> 01:41:42.336
Answer me!

1065
01:41:44.762 --> 01:41:46.027
SAFWAN: Your answer...

1066
01:41:46.470 --> 01:41:49.764
...is right outside the window.

1067
01:42:19.273 --> 01:42:23.153
Your faith says a man
is judged by his actions.

1068
01:42:24.067 --> 01:42:26.433
And what truer way to measure a man...

1069
01:42:27.126 --> 01:42:28.671
...than through what gives.

1070
01:42:30.278 --> 01:42:31.319
So there she is...

1071
01:42:33.083 --> 01:42:35.070
...my single act morality.

1072
01:42:50.137 --> 01:42:51.958
BILAL: Don't let it be your last.

1073
01:43:01.032 --> 01:43:01.612
BILAL: Ghufaira!

1074
01:43:03.023 --> 01:43:04.910
GHUFAIRA: Bilal! (cries)

1075
01:43:32.345 --> 01:43:33.993
KID: Give way, give way!

1076
01:43:34.827 --> 01:43:36.405
He's about to call out to Mecca!

1077
01:43:45.541 --> 01:43:54.196
<i>(chants & cheers)</i>

1078
01:44:44.732 --> 01:44:46.521
MOTHER: <i>What do you want to be when you grow up, Bilal?</i>

1079
01:44:48.222 --> 01:44:48.854


1080
01:44:51.225 --> 01:44:52.606


1081
01:44:59.568 --> 01:45:01.808


1082
01:45:08.588 --> 01:45:21.253


1083
01:45:21.600 --> 01:45:26.198
# Ooh... Oh, oh #

1084
01:45:26.276 --> 01:45:29.164
# Yeah #

1085
01:45:36.364 --> 01:45:38.868
# I was running away from myself #

1086
01:45:40.167 --> 01:45:42.910
# Had a barrel inside of my head #

1087
01:45:43.606 --> 01:45:47.000
# I was lyin' awake in my bed #

1088
01:45:47.001 --> 01:45:50.001
# Thinking 'bout all the things that you said #

1089
01:45:50.910 --> 01:45:54.100
# But now I'm stronger, I'm so much stronger #

1090
01:45:54.500 --> 01:45:58.100
# No more running, not any longer #

1091
01:45:58.500 --> 01:46:02.500
# And now I'm stronger, and finally I can say #

1092
01:46:02.900 --> 01:46:05.900
# That I'm not afraid... Yeah #

1093
01:47:00.928 --> 01:47:15.276
Translation and synchronizing
<font color="#F76541">  Ikraam </font>
